# Object-oriented: named objects with mutable state accessed through
# get/set rather than passed around explicitly. `new` creates the
# object; `send` mutates a field on it; `get` reads a field back --
# the object's own count survives between calls, unlike the pure
# functional style next door.
new("Counter", "c1")
send("c1", "set", "count", 0)
send("c1", "set", "count", get("c1", "count") + 1)
send("c1", "set", "count", get("c1", "count") + 1)
print(get("c1", "count"))
